    "expected_mechanism": "saturate at 80% steer for 300 ms right at curve entry. The fault starts just before the curve, putting the vehicle near the lateral acceleration limit (v^2*|kappa| close to 4.41*0.6). After the switch, LQR must counteract the residual steer offset. At moderate speed (30 km/h) and reduced friction (0.6), the LQR's fixed gains are expected to have enough margin to recover unless the initial error is large. This candidate sits near the boundary where the initial error state and the 90 deg/s rate limit of LQR will decide if recovery succeeds or fails.",
    "expected_side": "boundary",
