    "expected_mechanism": "solver_fail at the apex of a high-speed (40 km/h) low-friction (0.3) curve. The nominal lateral acceleration v^2*|kappa| at 40 km/h on friction 0.3 is well below the P-02 limit (4.41*0.3 ≈ 1.32 m/s²), but the solver failure removes the MPC output entirely. The switch happens immediately, and LQR must take over with a large cross-track error that may have grown during the fault. This candidate sits on the boundary between 'switch happened but LQR cannot reduce error fast enough' and 'recovery succeeds because the error was still within LQR's linear model range at the moment of switch.'",
    "expected_side": "boundary",
